From c784cc8e5b199f2830d45a3dd1de12d9aef026a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 01:47:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Kernels: derivatives of the unknowns and fused action of the
 tangent operator

- computeUnknownsDerivatives: the derivatives of the unknowns with respect
  to the reference coordinates are computed by a kernel from the gradients
  of the shape functions (mfem::DofToQuad), instead of the generic
  non-tensor path of mfem::QuadratureInterpolator, which was the main cost
  of the computations by kernels on simplices (beam on the GPU: 39 us
  instead of 890 us per call). The support check of the kernels no longer
  refers to the quadrature interpolator.
- addTangentOperatorAction: the action of the tangent operator without
  assembly is computed by one kernel per material and one thread per
  element, from the increments of the unknowns given element by element:
  increments of the gradients, of the thermodynamic forces and
  contribution B^T K B x w det J, without intermediate arrays at the
  points. It replaces computeGradientsIncrements,
  multiplyByTangentOperatorBlocks and the inner forces kernel in the
  action (beam on the GPU: 128 us per material instead of 350 us).
  AbstractBehaviourIntegrator::addTangentOperatorActionByKernels takes the
  increments of the unknowns element by element.
